# Database migrations

Alembic revisions live in `migrations/versions`. Update the SQLAlchemy models,
generate a revision, and review it before applying it:

```powershell
docker compose -f backend\docker-compose.yml run --build --rm migrate alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe the schema change"
```

Apply pending revisions with:

```powershell
docker compose -f backend\docker-compose.yml run --rm migrate alembic upgrade head
```

The Compose `migrate` service runs `alembic upgrade head` after Postgres is
healthy and before the API or Celery worker starts. Do not edit an already
applied revision; create a new revision for subsequent schema changes.
